$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{x^4+2x^3+x^2}{x+1}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{x^2(x+1)(x+1)}{(x+1)}\qquad\gray{\text{Factor numerator & denominator}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{{x^2}\cancel{(x+1)}(x+1)}{{}\cancel{(x+1)}}\qquad\gray{\text{Cancel out common factors}}
\\\\
&=x^3+x^2, \text{ for }x\neq -1
\end{align}$
